I'm curious, but how is MR so easy to get in the early game?  An
artifact implies an early wish, and given an early wish, I'd
prefer MR *and* a significantly lowered AC; i.e. GDSM.

This is one point I've not been able to follow in your
reasoning.  You list a lot of artifacts, etc.  In most of my
games, the only artifacts I'll have are the ones I've been given
for a sacrifice, and the quest artifact.  I often don't get a
wish until I've already a couple of artifacts, which means that
wishing for artifacts doesn't work.  If I get a wand of wishing
early on, then fine, but an early wand of wishing is very, very
rare in my games.

    [...]
> 7. I can't really see me casting spells, can someone reassure
> me of this being possible with a Valk?

I regularly spellcast as a Valk, or even as a Barb.  The higher
level spells aren't necessarily available, or reliable, but
magic missle and cure sickness are available, and some of the
higher level ones as well, if you can afford to try them several
times.  (E.g. magic mapping: if it doesn't work, try again.  But
don't count on touch of death to escape in a tight spot.)

> 8. I don't really need a Self-Notes.txt file for files; I've
> tried it before and it makes the game more laboured without
> much of a payoff.

It depends on the degree.  I do keep notes with regards to the
levels I've encountered things on (altar on level 2), but not
much else.

> 9. "In some of your later posts, you seemed overly concerned
